    <div class="grid-3">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="tag">Business AI • Design in progress</span>
        <h3>Inbox-to-Action</h3>
        <p>Turn Outlook email and calendar activity into an action brief, meeting preparation, and reviewable drafts.</p>
        <p><strong>Control:</strong> read-only intake; a person approves every external action.</p>
        <p><strong>What to measure:</strong> missed commitments, draft corrections, and verified review time.</p>
        <a class="link" href="/work/inbox-to-action/">See the workflow design →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="tag">Custom solution • Illustrative</span>
        <h3>Knowledge-to-Decision</h3>
        <p>A proposed internal assistant that retrieves approved business documents and returns source-linked answers.</p>
        <p><strong>Control:</strong> enforce document access in retrieval, test grounding, and require approval before writes.</p>
        <p><strong>What to measure:</strong> answer quality, access leakage, latency, and cost per useful answer.</p>
        <a class="link" href="/work/private-azure-ai-platform/#application">Explore the application pattern →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="tag">Enterprise • Reference design</span>
        <h3>Private Azure AI Platform</h3>
        <p>A foundation for multiple governed workloads, with separate environments, private service access, and controlled delivery.</p>
        <p><strong>Control:</strong> identity, network boundaries, infrastructure review, and recovery plans.</p>
        <p><strong>What to measure:</strong> deployment repeatability, recovery, throughput, and operating cost.</p>
